# PATH-HEAD-WRITE-READ-AS-CALL (steps/defects.md): `node\A: B` writes the
# existing field A of the space above the method after ordinary admission
# (L3 §9); it is not a call of node\A with B as its argument. Executing the
# field would be `call: node\A`. After swap the unit field A holds B. Entry 7.
A:
    int: mark 1
end: A
B:
    int: mark 2
end: B
fn: swap () int
    node\A: B
    return: 0
end: swap
int: s swap()
int: m A\mark
int: ok 81
if: m = 2
    ok: 7
sendMessage: exit(exit_code: ok; stdout: ""; stderr: "")
return
